{"kind":"request","text":"Planner: decide how the integration branch request/test-overhead reaches main while declared acts stage 3's condition 2 is open. This owes a decision only: no Git artifact, no landing.\n\nThe facts. Main is e6e67828 and has stage 1 only. The branch composes stage 2 (approved 9cb05da9 at 39430e23), stage 3 (changes requested 6263fdec), stage 5 (in review at 736f4953), the MCP core (changes requested bc0d7f6b for the planner's contract artifacts and a dual binding), the bearer fix 5d41ea36 (in review at 87cd5804) and the test-overhead work (approved b1738122 at f6212850). Stage 3's review has two blocking items. One is delivered at a10c9bec: the legacy-recovery negative case now runs the whole verifier. The other is complete carry accounting. That needs the carry-pass amendment, which you returned with changes A to F (85032553), and then the prepared event, which stage 4 owns (48c021ea). So stage 3 cannot be approved in full until part of stage 4 is designed, reviewed and built.\n\nWhy this matters. My path dae9a1f3 was one landing when all four lanes are approved. Stage 3 cannot be left out cleanly: packages/log on main cannot read a v2 room's log, the Room's own tests publish and verify v2 logs, and artroom verify would fail every room that adopts declared acts. So as things stand, nothing lands until stage 4's prepared event and the pass events exist, and every other lane waits behind them.\n\nThe options I see.\n(1) Wait. Revise the amendment, get it adopted, build prepared and the pass events under stages 3 and 4, then land everything.\n(2) Land the branch when stage 2, stage 5, the MCP core and 5d41ea36 hold approvals and stage 3 holds an approval of what it delivers, with condition 2's complete accounting recorded as open on request 1e8fee4b, which stays open and promised. Main's verifier would then do everything it does on the branch: it refuses a reservation with an open obligation and a carry that skipped a newer check, and it says in its report what it cannot prove.\n(3) A separable composition without stage 3. I do not think this exists, for the reason above.\n\nMy recommendation is (2). What a verifier on main could not yet detect is a missing carry judgment that did not carry when nothing later carried. That cannot admit a landing (notes/2026-10-03-carry-accounting.md, \"What an omission can do\"), the Room's fences are in and approved, and the gap is disclosed in verify's own output. Against that, (1) holds the generic client, the MCP core and Room admission by declaration off main for the length of a stage 4 design. But the checker's verdict says no reduced acceptance is adopted, so this is not mine to choose.","body":{"conditions":"(1) A decision between waiting and landing with stage 3's condition 2 open, or another route, with reasons. (2) If landing with it open: what stage 3's review must bind for that landing (which conditions, at which head), and how the open remainder stays owed and visible. (3) If waiting: the order of the amendment, stage 4's prepared event and the pass events, and who owns each.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}